Using Amazon Web Services, create and deploy a simple static website using Amazon
S3.
Tasks to be Performed
1. Create an S3 bucket for website hosting.
2. Configure the bucket for static website hosting.
3. Upload the following files:
o index.html (main webpage)
o At least one image file
4. Apply a bucket policy to enable public access.
5. Set the index document as index.html.
6. Access the website using the generated S3 endpoint URL.
7. Verify that the website loads correctly with all resources.

1. Login to AWS Console
Open
AWS Console
Login to your AWS account.
2. Open Amazon S3

In top search bar type:

S3
Open
Amazon Simple Storage Service
3. Create S3 Bucket
Open Buckets
Left sidebar → Buckets

Click:

Create bucket
Configure Bucket
Bucket Name

Enter unique name.

Example:

sahil-static-website-demo
Region

Choose nearest region.

Example:

Asia Pacific (Mumbai) ap-south-1
4. Disable Public Access Block

Scroll to:

Block Public Access settings for this bucket
Untick

Untick:

Block all public access
Acknowledge Warning

Tick:

I acknowledge that the current settings might result in this bucket and the objects within becoming public.
5. Create Bucket

Click:

Create bucket

Bucket created successfully.

6. Open Bucket

Click your bucket name:

sahil-static-website-demo
7. Create index.html File

Create a file on your computer named:

index.html

Add this code:

<html>
<head>
    <title>My AWS Website</title>
</head>
<body>
    <h1>Welcome to My Static Website</h1>
    <p>Website hosted using Amazon S3</p>

    <img src="image.jpg" width="300">
</body>
</html>

Save the file.

8. Upload Website Files
Upload Files

Inside bucket click:

Upload

Click:

Add files
Select:
index.html
one image file

Example image:

image.jpg
Upload

Click:

Upload

Files uploaded successfully.

9. Enable Static Website Hosting
Open Properties Tab

Inside bucket open:

Properties
Static Website Hosting

Scroll to:

Static website hosting

Click:

Edit
Enable Hosting

Select:

Enable
Hosting Type

Choose:

Host a static website
Index Document

Enter:

index.html
Save

Click:

Save changes
10. Apply Bucket Policy for Public Access
Open Permissions Tab

Open:

Permissions
Bucket Policy

Scroll to:

Bucket policy

Click:

Edit
Paste Policy

Replace bucket name with your bucket name.

Example:

{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Sid": "PublicReadGetObject",
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Principal": "*",
      "Action": "s3:GetObject",
      "Resource": "arn:aws:s3:::sahil-static-website-demo/*"
    }
  ]
}
Save Policy

Click:

Save changes
11. Get Website Endpoint URL
Open Properties

Go to:

Properties

Scroll to:

Static website hosting
Copy Endpoint

You will see:

Bucket website endpoint

Example:

http://sahil-static-website-demo.s3-website.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com

Copy the URL.

12. Access Website
Open new browser tab
Paste endpoint URL
Press Enter
13. Verify Website

Expected Result:

✅ Webpage loads successfully
✅ Text is displayed
✅ Image loads correctly
